# Extracted game data is NOT redistributed. Per ADR-0014 and 03-data-ingestion.md §7,
# extraction from a game you own supports a personal tool; republishing it as a dataset
# is a different act. This repo is public, so all game-derived content stays local and
# is regenerated by running tools/ingest against your own install.
data/raw/
data/1.0.2/
data/*.csv
# Card artwork is game art, not extracted facts, so it is the clearest case of all:
# the map basemaps and Pal icons are Pocketpair's, decoded from a pak you own for a
# tool that runs on your machine. Regenerated by tools/ingest/build_assets.py.
data/*/assets/

# Voice recordings for the STT evaluation. Personal data, and this repo is public.
data/stt_eval/*/
!data/stt_eval/prompts.json

# Captured gameplay sessions: the clip of every utterance, plus the routing log. Same
# rule as the eval recordings above and MORE so - capture records whatever is near the
# microphone, including other people in the room, which is why both its flags default
# off. This entry was missing until 2026-08-11 because capture had never been switched
# on, so it had never produced a file to catch; 42 clips were committed before anyone
# noticed. The pattern that guards personal data has to exist before the feature that
# creates it, not after.
data/sessions/
# Cached transcriptions from the hotword sweep. Derived from those recordings and
# regenerated by tools/eval/score_hotwords.py, so it belongs with them rather than in
# the repo - the pattern above only covers the per-condition directories.
data/stt_eval/*.json
!data/stt_eval/prompts.json

# Local config: contains absolute paths to the game install and save directory
config.local.*
.env
*.secrets.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# .NET
bin/
obj/

# pytest
.pytest_cache/
Notes/
# Who each Discord user is in the game. Holds Discord user ids - never committed.
data/players.json

# The bot heartbeat and its captured startup output. Runtime state, not source.
data/bot-state.json
data/bot.log
